   "text": {
    "L1": "After thousands come lakhs and crores in the Indian system.",
    "L2": "One lakh is 1,00,000, and one crore is 1,00,00,000.",
    "L3": "One lakh equals 100 thousand. One crore equals 100 lakh, or 10 million.",
    "L4": "So the belief that one crore equals one million is not true. One crore is ten million.",
    "L5": "In Indian commas, group the first three digits from the right, then group digits in pairs.",
    "L6": "For example, seven crore three lakh fifty thousand is 7,03,50,000.",
    "L7": "Regrouping in threes gives 70,350,000, or 70.35 million.",
    "L8": "The commas and names change between systems, but the number itself stays the same.",
    "L9": "Now tap the value equal to one crore."
   },
